{"card":{"card_id":"ma-c-4855a6e6b08d055c3bff","statement":"A $\\ga$-module $E$ is called a Whittaker module if $a\n-\\chi(a)$, $\\forall a \\in \\m$, acts on $E$ locally nilpotently. A Whittaker vector in a Whittaker $\\ga$-module $E$ is a vector $x \\in E$ which satisfies $(a -\\chi(a)) x=0, \\forall a \\in \\m. $\n\nLet $\\whmod$ be the category of finitely generated Whittaker $\\ga$-modules.","source_id":"arXiv:0912.0689","cluster":"representation_theory","statement_sha256":"a7a924c4e22aaba20faaf4698fc8589682b123645a2547813b4d080780262102","kind":"definition","label":"Definition 34","ref_key":"W:def:Whit","name":"","order":41,"deps":[],"cite_keys":[],"provenance":{"source_url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/0912.0689","harvest_mode":"arxiv_eprint","payload_sha256":"4f5174c21e23be19ab8bd2dad075272b9ecc3d5bdb229e520b493f9160fc8027","line":1714,"origin":"latex_env","retrieved_at":"2026-09-26T15:07:51+08:00"},"wash":{"version":"cardwash.v3","stages":["segment","purify","classify","dedupe","emit"],"numbering":"document_order_with_label_heuristic","detail":{"stripped_proof":false,"chars":322,"math_hints":36}}},"paper":{"source_id":"arXiv:0912.0689","title":"Nilpotent orbits and finite $W$-algebras","abstract":"In recent years, the finite W-algebras associated to a semisimple Lie algebra and its nilpotent element have been studied intensively from different viewpoints. In this lecture series, we shall present some basic constructions, connections, and applications of finite W-algebras.","authors":["Weiqiang Wang"],"year":"2009","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/0912.0689","cluster":"representation_theory","macros":{"ad":"\\text{ad}\\,","Ad":"\\text{Ad}\\,","brst":"\\mathcal{B}^\\bullet","c":"\\mathfrak c","C":"\\mathbb C","col":"\\text{col}","End":"\\text{End}","ev":"{#1}_{\\bar{0}}","od":"{#1}_{\\bar{1}}","ga":"\\mathfrak{g}","Ga":"\\Gamma","gl":"\\mathfrak{gl}","gr":"\\text{gr}","Hom":"\\text{Hom}","hf":"\\frac12","lag":"\\mathfrak{l}","la":"\\lambda","m":"\\mathfrak m","a":"\\ma